 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S442-011\", \"clauses\": {\"solve_subtraction\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F09\", \"template\": \"Taking away {b} {name}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F09 states the subtraction operation as the question text, with b drawn from the repeated generated value b (printed runs 1 to 3, 10, 12, 15) and the noun from _EMOJI_NAMES or its plural. The minuend is carried by F10 (a), so the problem as a whole is a subtraction problem.\"}, \"in_pictures\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F10\", \"template\": \"{group} — There {verb} {a} {name}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F10 prints its group as a row of emoji from nested families F12 to F21, which is the picture representation the clause names.\"}, \"less_than_20\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F10\", \"template\": \"{group} — There {verb} {a} {name}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F10 prints a with printed runs 1 to 6, 10 to 15, all below 20, and the declared number_range 20 variant exists. The clause is producible through F10's a. Observed values never reach 16 to 19, which is a coverage note rather than a missing producible route.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F03\", \"F04\", \"F07\", \"F08\", \"F09\", \"F10\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Subtract the ones: {oa} − {ob} = {od}.\", \"Subtract the tens: {ta} − {tb} = {td}.{note}\", \"How many {names} are left?\", \"Taking away 0 {names}.\", \"Taking away {b} {name}.\", \"{group} — There {verb} {a} {name}.\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F03 (hints): oa and ob are computed from the ones digits of a and b, with no ordering constraint between them, so the ones difference can be negative (a from 10 to 15 with b of 3 gives a ones difference of 1 minus 3). The hint would then print a negative result as the 'Subtract the ones' step, which is wrong procedure and a concept beyond grade 1 Q3. F04 (hints): the note slot is one of the generator's own choices with no tie to whether a ten was borrowed, so ' (1 ten became 10 ones)' can print on a problem with no borrow; and the member ' (after regrouping)' uses 'regrouping', which is listed in NOT_YET_KNOWN, so the template fails the vocabulary gate on every render that picks it. F07, F08 and F09 (question text): the noun slot is 'a noun from a fixed list, or its plural' with no tie to the count, so singular forms can print with plural 'are' or with numbers other than 1 (for example the singular form inside 'How many {names} are left?' or 'Taking away 0 {names}.'), which is ungrammatical text for a grade 1 learner. F10 (question text): the group is nested learner text from F12 to F21 chosen with no tie to a, and the name and the copula are not tied to a; the picture can show a count different from a, a name unrelated to the picture, and 'is' or 'are' independent of a, so the printed sentence can state a wrong count. Families F01, F02, F05, F06, F11 and F12 to F21 were checked and not flagged: F02 prints counting back from 10 by 1 to 3, F06 and F05 print results observed from 0 to 14 with no negative results, F01 is gated to the word difference, which is in cumulative_vocab, and F11 prints option letters only.\"}",
